115%;
font-family:"Aptos",sans-serif;color:#1E6A73'>10.3 Expanded road</span></h2>

<p class=3DMsoNormal style=3D'margin-bottom:5.0pt;line-height:107%'>When se=
lected,
the ribbon should unfold into a route road made of visually distinct road
blocks. Each block represents a major step. The user can understand the jou=
rney
at a glance and then widen or expand a block to inspect its fields.</p>

<h2 style=3D'margin-top:7.0pt;margin-right:0cm;margin-bottom:4.0pt;margin-l=
eft:
0cm'><span style=3D'font-size:12.5pt;mso-bidi-font-size:13.0pt;line-height:=
115%;
font-family:"Aptos",sans-serif;color:#1E6A73'>10.4 Color meaning</span></h2>

<p class=3DMsoNormal style=3D'margin-bottom:5.0pt;line-height:107%'>Color s=
hould
communicate the category of work rather than being randomly assigned. For
example, documentation, language/testing, university/admission, funding,
immigration/visa and travel may use distinct visual categories. Text and ic=
ons
should accompany color so the meaning does not depend on color alone.</p>

<h1 style=3D'margin-top:11.0pt;margin-right:0cm;margin-bottom:4.0pt;margin-=
left:
0cm'><span style=3D'font-size:16.0pt;mso-bidi-font-size:14.0pt;line-height:=
115%;
font-family:"Aptos",sans-serif;color:#18324A'>11. Route Structure and Step
Information</span></h1>

<p class=3DMsoNormal style=3D'margin-bottom:5.0pt;line-height:107%'>Each ro=
ute is
composed of ordered or partially overlapping steps. A step may represent a
mandatory action, optional action, waiting period, decision, test, document
process, application, funding action, immigration action or travel stage.</=
p>

