font-family:"Aptos",sans-serif;color:#1E6A73'>12.2 No evidence requirement<=
/span></h2>

<p class=3DMsoNormal style=3D'margin-bottom:5.0pt;line-height:107%'>The pla=
tform is
not intended to verify whether the user genuinely completed IELTS, received
admission, submitted a visa or completed another step. The tracker is for t=
he
user=92s own benefit. Therefore the user should not be asked to upload supp=
orting
evidence merely to mark a personal step complete.</p>

<h2 style=3D'margin-top:7.0pt;margin-right:0cm;margin-bottom:4.0pt;margin-l=
eft:
0cm'><span style=3D'font-size:12.5pt;mso-bidi-font-size:13.0pt;line-height:=
115%;
font-family:"Aptos",sans-serif;color:#1E6A73'>12.3 Privacy of progress</spa=
n></h2>

<p class=3DMsoNormal style=3D'margin-bottom:5.0pt;line-height:107%'>Other u=
sers
must not be able to see an individual user=92s journey progress, notes, tar=
get
dates, scores or completion status. Public statistics may use aggregated
signals only where they do not expose private individual progress.</p>

<h1 style=3D'margin-top:11.0pt;margin-right:0cm;margin-bottom:4.0pt;margin-=
left:
0cm'><span style=3D'font-size:16.0pt;mso-bidi-font-size:14.0pt;line-height:=
115%;
font-family:"Aptos",sans-serif;color:#18324A'>13. Live Route Evolution and
Change Propagation</span></h1>

<p class=3DMsoNormal style=3D'margin-bottom:5.0pt;line-height:107%'>A route=
 must
remain capable of changing after users begin following it. Community updates
should improve the live public route while preserving earlier states.</p>

<h2 style=3D'margin-top:7.0pt;margin-right:0cm;margin-bottom:4.0pt;margin-l=
eft:
0cm'><span style=3D'font-size:12.5pt;mso-bidi-font-size:13.0pt;line-height:=
115%;
font-family:"Aptos",sans-serif;color:#1E6A73'>13.1 Effect on followers</spa=
n></h2>

<p class=3DMsoNormal style=3D'margin-bottom:5.0pt;line-height:107%'>When th=
e live
route changes, users following the route should see that new information
exists. The platform should emphasize changes affecting unfinished or upcom=
ing
steps rather than forcing the user to reread the entire route.</p>

<h2 style=3D'margin-top:7.0pt;margin-right:0cm;margin-bottom:4.0pt;margin-l=
eft:
0cm'><span style=3D'font-size:12.5pt;mso-bidi-font-size:13.0pt;line-height:=
115%;
font-family:"Aptos",sans-serif;color:#1E6A73'>13.2 Personal data is not
overwritten</span></h2>

<p class=3DMsoNormal style=3D'margin-bottom:5.0pt;line-height:107%'>A publi=
c change
must not silently erase a user=92s private progress or notes. If the user
completed a step before a requirement changed, the journey should preserve =
that
completion and explain that the public route changed after the user=92s rec=
orded
date.</p>

<h2 style=3D'margin-top:7.0pt;margin-right:0cm;margin-bottom:4.0pt;margin-l=
eft:
0cm'><span style=3D'font-size:12.5pt;mso-bidi-font-size:13.0pt;line-height:=
115%;
font-family:"Aptos",sans-serif;color:#1E6A73'>13.3 User control over
applicability</span></h2>

<p class=3DMsoNormal style=3D'margin-bottom:5.0pt;line-height:107%'>Where t=
he
platform cannot confidently determine whether a rule change applies to a
follower, the follower should be shown the change and allowed to mark it as
applicable, already handled, or not applicable to their case.</p>

