<p class=3DMsoNormal style=3D'margin-bottom:2.0pt'><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></p>

<h2 style=3D'margin-top:7.0pt;margin-right:0cm;margin-bottom:4.0pt;margin-l=
eft:
0cm'><span style=3D'font-size:12.5pt;mso-bidi-font-size:13.0pt;line-height:=
115%;
font-family:"Aptos",sans-serif;color:#1E6A73'>16.1 ADD</span></h2>

<p class=3DMsoNormal style=3D'margin-bottom:5.0pt;line-height:107%'>Create a
missing route, add a missing step, or add a missing field within a step.</p>

<h2 style=3D'margin-top:7.0pt;margin-right:0cm;margin-bottom:4.0pt;margin-l=
eft:
0cm'><span style=3D'font-size:12.5pt;mso-bidi-font-size:13.0pt;line-height:=
115%;
font-family:"Aptos",sans-serif;color:#1E6A73'>16.2 UPDATE</span></h2>

<p class=3DMsoNormal style=3D'margin-bottom:5.0pt;line-height:107%'>Provide=
 a newer
or corrected value for existing information. An update creates a new revisi=
on
and does not permanently destroy the old value.</p>

<h2 style=3D'margin-top:7.0pt;margin-right:0cm;margin-bottom:4.0pt;margin-l=
eft:
0cm'><span style=3D'font-size:12.5pt;mso-bidi-font-size:13.0pt;line-height:=
115%;
font-family:"Aptos",sans-serif;color:#1E6A73'>16.3 CONFIRM</span></h2>

<p class=3DMsoNormal style=3D'margin-bottom:5.0pt;line-height:107%'>Indicat=
e that
information was still current or matched the contributor=92s recent experie=
nce.
Confirmations are essential because silence does not prove that old informa=
tion
remains accurate.</p>

<h2 style=3D'margin-top:7.0pt;margin-right:0cm;margin-bottom:4.0pt;margin-l=
eft:
0cm'><span style=3D'font-size:12.5pt;mso-bidi-font-size:13.0pt;line-height:=
115%;
font-family:"Aptos",sans-serif;color:#1E6A73'>16.4 CHALLENGE</span></h2>

<p class=3DMsoNormal style=3D'margin-bottom:5.0pt;line-height:107%'>Mark
information as obsolete, incorrect, misleading, incomplete, suspicious or
otherwise in need of review. Challenges should capture reason where possible
rather than acting as a generic dislike button.</p>

<h2 style=3D'margin-top:7.0pt;margin-right:0cm;margin-bottom:4.0pt;margin-l=
eft:
0cm'><span style=3D'font-size:12.5pt;mso-bidi-font-size:13.0pt;line-height:=
115%;
font-family:"Aptos",sans-serif;color:#1E6A73'>16.5 Contribution at the right
moment</span></h2>

<p class=3DMsoNormal style=3D'margin-bottom:5.0pt;line-height:107%'>The pla=
tform
should encourage contribution immediately after a follower marks a step
complete, because this is when firsthand knowledge is freshest. A lightweig=
ht
prompt such as =93Was this step still accurate?=94 can generate confirmatio=
ns or
corrections without requiring a separate contribution campaign.</p>

<h1 style=3D'margin-top:11.0pt;margin-right:0cm;margin-bottom:4.0pt;margin-=
left:
0cm'><span style=3D'font-size:16.0pt;mso-bidi-font-size:14.0pt;line-height:=
115%;
font-family:"Aptos",sans-serif;color:#18324A'>17. Field Revision, Archival =
and
Non-Destructive Editing</span></h1>

<h2 style=3D'margin-top:7.0pt;margin-right:0cm;margin-bottom:4.0pt;margin-l=
eft:
0cm'><span style=3D'font-size:12.5pt;mso-bidi-font-size:13.0pt;line-height:=
115%;
font-family:"Aptos",sans-serif;color:#1E6A73'>17.1 No normal-user deletion<=
/span></h2>

<p class=3DMsoNormal style=3D'margin-bottom:5.0pt;line-height:107%'>Ordinary
contributors should not have a direct destructive delete function for shared
route knowledge. They may update a field or challenge it as obsolete, incor=
rect
or unsafe.</p>

<h2 style=3D'margin-top:7.0pt;margin-right:0cm;margin-bottom:4.0pt;margin-l=
eft:
0cm'><span style=3D'font-size:12.5pt;mso-bidi-font-size:13.0pt;line-height:=
115%;
font-family:"Aptos",sans-serif;color:#1E6A73'>17.2 Revision history</span><=
/h2>

<p class=3DMsoNormal style=3D'margin-bottom:5.0pt;line-height:107%'>Every
meaningful update should preserve the prior value. If multiple contributors
change a field over time, the history should remain visible so that mistakes
can be reversed and contradictory periods can be understood.</p>

<h2 style=3D'margin-top:7.0pt;margin-right:0cm;margin-bottom:4.0pt;margin-l=
eft:
0cm'><span style=3D'font-size:12.5pt;mso-bidi-font-size:13.0pt;line-height:=
115%;
font-family:"Aptos",sans-serif;color:#1E6A73'>17.3 Archiving obsolete field=
s</span></h2>

<p class=3DMsoNormal style=3D'margin-bottom:5.0pt;line-height:107%'>A field=
 that is
no longer needed may be challenged as obsolete. Once community signals or
moderation determine that it should not remain current, it becomes archived
rather than erased. Archived information should normally disappear from the
main current view but remain available in history.</p>

