<h2 style=3D'margin-top:7.0pt;margin-right:0cm;margin-bottom:4.0pt;margin-l=
eft:
0cm'><span style=3D'font-size:12.5pt;mso-bidi-font-size:13.0pt;line-height:=
115%;
font-family:"Aptos",sans-serif;color:#1E6A73'>17.5 Frequently edited
information</span></h2>

<p class=3DMsoNormal style=3D'margin-bottom:5.0pt;line-height:107%'>If a fi=
eld is
changed repeatedly in a short period or receives conflicting
confirmations/challenges, the product should communicate that volatility to
readers rather than presenting the newest value as unquestioned truth.</p>

<h1 style=3D'margin-top:11.0pt;margin-right:0cm;margin-bottom:4.0pt;margin-=
left:
0cm'><span style=3D'font-size:16.0pt;mso-bidi-font-size:14.0pt;line-height:=
115%;
font-family:"Aptos",sans-serif;color:#18324A'>18. Route Creation, Identity,
Duplication and Merging</span></h1>

<h2 style=3D'margin-top:7.0pt;margin-right:0cm;margin-bottom:4.0pt;margin-l=
eft:
0cm'><span style=3D'font-size:12.5pt;mso-bidi-font-size:13.0pt;line-height:=
115%;
font-family:"Aptos",sans-serif;color:#1E6A73'>18.1 Community-created routes=
</span></h2>

<p class=3DMsoNormal style=3D'margin-bottom:5.0pt;line-height:107%'>Signed-=
in
contributors should be able to create routes that do not yet exist. Newly
created routes must not automatically look as mature as established routes.
They begin with a visible developing/experimental status until they gain
meaningful use, sources, confirmations or community activity.</p>

<h2 style=3D'margin-top:7.0pt;margin-right:0cm;margin-bottom:4.0pt;margin-l=
eft:
0cm'><span style=3D'font-size:12.5pt;mso-bidi-font-size:13.0pt;line-height:=
115%;
font-family:"Aptos",sans-serif;color:#1E6A73'>18.2 Multiple valid routes</s=
pan></h2>

<p class=3DMsoNormal style=3D'margin-bottom:5.0pt;line-height:107%'>Multipl=
e routes
for the same origin and destination are acceptable when their journey diffe=
rs
materially in process, timing, scholarship mechanism, institution-specific
pathway or other meaningful content. The road itself may therefore look
different in sequence, duration and information.</p>

<h2 style=3D'margin-top:7.0pt;margin-right:0cm;margin-bottom:4.0pt;margin-l=
eft:
0cm'><span style=3D'font-size:12.5pt;mso-bidi-font-size:13.0pt;line-height:=
115%;
font-family:"Aptos",sans-serif;color:#1E6A73'>18.3 Permanent route identity=
</span></h2>

<p class=3DMsoNormal style=3D'margin-bottom:5.0pt;line-height:107%'>Althoug=
h users
recognize routes through their visual road and content, every route must
conceptually remain a distinct persistent object so followers, history,
revisions and archival actions stay attached to the correct route. The
implementation method is outside the scope of this document.</p>

<h2 style=3D'margin-top:7.0pt;margin-right:0cm;margin-bottom:4.0pt;margin-l=
eft:
0cm'><span style=3D'font-size:12.5pt;mso-bidi-font-size:13.0pt;line-height:=
115%;
font-family:"Aptos",sans-serif;color:#1E6A73'>18.4 Duplicate routes</span><=
/h2>

<p class=3DMsoNormal style=3D'margin-bottom:5.0pt;line-height:107%'>A new r=
oute
that substantially duplicates an existing route should be discouraged from
unnecessary duplication and may later be merged. Route merging should prese=
rve
the followers=92 private journeys and historical contributions rather than
causing data loss.</p>

<h2 style=3D'margin-top:7.0pt;margin-right:0cm;margin-bottom:4.0pt;margin-l=
eft:
0cm'><span style=3D'font-size:12.5pt;mso-bidi-font-size:13.0pt;line-height:=
115%;
font-family:"Aptos",sans-serif;color:#1E6A73'>18.5 No route ownership</span=
></h2>

<p class=3DMsoNormal style=3D'margin-bottom:5.0pt;line-height:107%'>A route=
 creator
contributes the first version but does not own the shared route. The commun=
ity
must be able to improve it even if the creator becomes inactive or disagrees
with later corrections.</p>

<h1 style=3D'margin-top:11.0pt;margin-right:0cm;margin-bottom:4.0pt;margin-=
left:
0cm'><span style=3D'font-size:16.0pt;mso-bidi-font-size:14.0pt;line-height:=
115%;
font-family:"Aptos",sans-serif;color:#18324A'>19. Route Lifecycle, Activity=
 and
Freshness</span></h1>

<p class=3DMsoNormal style=3D'margin-bottom:5.0pt;line-height:107%'>Activit=
y is an
important signal but not proof of correctness. A route may receive little
activity simply because it is seasonal or less popular. The platform should
therefore treat inactivity as a freshness warning rather than immediate
evidence that the route is false.</p>

