115%;
font-family:"Aptos",sans-serif;color:#1E6A73'>21.1 Route confidence</span><=
/h2>

<p class=3DMsoNormal style=3D'margin-bottom:5.0pt;line-height:107%'>The pla=
tform
may communicate route confidence or maturity using combined signals such as
age, sources, confirmations, contributor history, recent activity, unresolv=
ed
challenges and follower use. Popularity alone must not be treated as proof =
of
correctness.</p>

<h2 style=3D'margin-top:7.0pt;margin-right:0cm;margin-bottom:4.0pt;margin-l=
eft:
0cm'><span style=3D'font-size:12.5pt;mso-bidi-font-size:13.0pt;line-height:=
115%;
font-family:"Aptos",sans-serif;color:#1E6A73'>21.2 Route passport / route
history summary</span></h2>

<p class=3DMsoNormal style=3D'margin-bottom:5.0pt;line-height:107%'>A route=
 may
expose an at-a-glance history such as created date, follower count, contrib=
utor
count, change count, last meaningful change, last confirmation, number of
sources and unresolved reports. This gives readers context before relying on
the route.</p>

<h1 style=3D'margin-top:11.0pt;margin-right:0cm;margin-bottom:4.0pt;margin-=
left:
0cm'><span style=3D'font-size:16.0pt;mso-bidi-font-size:14.0pt;line-height:=
115%;
font-family:"Aptos",sans-serif;color:#18324A'>22. Safety: Links, Contacts, =
Scam
and Abuse Controls</span></h1>

<p class=3DMsoNormal style=3D'margin-bottom:5.0pt;line-height:107%'>The pro=
ject is
motivated partly by the risk of scams and misinformation. The contribution
model must therefore be open without making arbitrary community links or
contact information immediately look trustworthy.</p>

