<h2 style=3D'margin-top:7.0pt;margin-right:0cm;margin-bottom:4.0pt;margin-l=
eft:
0cm'><span style=3D'font-size:12.5pt;mso-bidi-font-size:13.0pt;line-height:=
115%;
font-family:"Aptos",sans-serif;color:#1E6A73'>22.3 Contact information</spa=
n></h2>

<p class=3DMsoNormal style=3D'margin-bottom:5.0pt;line-height:107%'>Public =
contacts
may be contributed, but phone numbers and personal-looking contact details
carry harassment risk. New or changed contacts should display source and tr=
ust
information. Reports such as =93private person=92s number,=94 =93wrong cont=
act,=94
=93impersonation=94 or =93scam=94 should permit rapid hiding/quarantine whi=
le retaining
history for moderation.</p>

<h2 style=3D'margin-top:7.0pt;margin-right:0cm;margin-bottom:4.0pt;margin-l=
eft:
0cm'><span style=3D'font-size:12.5pt;mso-bidi-font-size:13.0pt;line-height:=
115%;
font-family:"Aptos",sans-serif;color:#1E6A73'>22.4 Payment and money-related
content</span></h2>

<p class=3DMsoNormal style=3D'margin-bottom:5.0pt;line-height:107%'>Payment
instructions, personal bank accounts, mobile-wallet numbers and similar con=
tent
are high risk. The platform should never make a community-submitted payment
instruction appear equivalent to an official institution payment channel. R=
oute
ranking or trust must never be purchasable.</p>

<h2 style=3D'margin-top:7.0pt;margin-right:0cm;margin-bottom:4.0pt;margin-l=
eft:
0cm'><span style=3D'font-size:12.5pt;mso-bidi-font-size:13.0pt;line-height:=
115%;
font-family:"Aptos",sans-serif;color:#1E6A73'>22.5 Adult, phishing and
malicious content</span></h2>

<p class=3DMsoNormal style=3D'margin-bottom:5.0pt;line-height:107%'>Because
arbitrary links can lead to phishing, pornography, malware or changed conte=
nt,
the safety principle is preventative: unknown links should not immediately
inherit trust simply because a signed-in user added them. Community reporti=
ng,
contributor reputation and quarantine should allow suspicious destinations =
to
be hidden quickly.</p>

<h1 style=3D'margin-top:11.0pt;margin-right:0cm;margin-bottom:4.0pt;margin-=
left:
0cm'><span style=3D'font-size:16.0pt;mso-bidi-font-size:14.0pt;line-height:=
115%;
font-family:"Aptos",sans-serif;color:#18324A'>23. Reporting and Moderation<=
/span></h1>

<h2 style=3D'margin-top:7.0pt;margin-right:0cm;margin-bottom:4.0pt;margin-l=
eft:
0cm'><span style=3D'font-size:12.5pt;mso-bidi-font-size:13.0pt;line-height:=
115%;
font-family:"Aptos",sans-serif;color:#1E6A73'>23.1 Reporting should be dist=
inct
from ordinary challenge</span></h2>

<p class=3DMsoNormal style=3D'margin-bottom:5.0pt;line-height:107%'>A routi=
ne
challenge means =93this information is no longer correct.=94 A report means=
 =93this
may be abusive or unsafe.=94 Reports should therefore support reasons such =
as
phishing/scam, adult content, malware/download, impersonation,
harassment/personal information, malicious contact, spam or other serious
concern.</p>

<h2 style=3D'margin-top:7.0pt;margin-right:0cm;margin-bottom:4.0pt;margin-l=
eft:
0cm'><span style=3D'font-size:12.5pt;mso-bidi-font-size:13.0pt;line-height:=
115%;
font-family:"Aptos",sans-serif;color:#1E6A73'>23.2 Temporary hiding /
quarantine</span></h2>

<p class=3DMsoNormal style=3D'margin-bottom:5.0pt;line-height:107%'>High-ri=
sk
content may be temporarily hidden or quarantined when credible reports reac=
h an
appropriate threshold. The administrator can then restore, correct, archive=
 or
remove the item. Exact thresholds are an operational decision and are not f=
ixed
in this concept baseline.</p>

<h2 style=3D'margin-top:7.0pt;margin-right:0cm;margin-bottom:4.0pt;margin-l=
eft:
0cm'><span style=3D'font-size:12.5pt;mso-bidi-font-size:13.0pt;line-height:=
115%;
font-family:"Aptos",sans-serif;color:#1E6A73'>23.3 Administrator role</span=
></h2>

<p class=3DMsoNormal style=3D'margin-bottom:5.0pt;line-height:107%'>The
administrator should not be expected to approve every normal contribution.
Manual intervention is primarily for safety, disputes, abuse, annual
maintenance and exceptional cases. The long-term objective is a community t=
hat
maintains ordinary route accuracy itself.</p>

<h1 style=3D'margin-top:11.0pt;margin-right:0cm;margin-bottom:4.0pt;margin-=
left:
0cm'><span style=3D'font-size:16.0pt;mso-bidi-font-size:14.0pt;line-height:=
115%;
font-family:"Aptos",sans-serif;color:#18324A'>24. Privacy and Minimal Perso=
nal
Data</span></h1>

<p class=3DMsoNormal style=3D'margin-bottom:5.0pt;line-height:107%'>The pla=
tform
should deliberately avoid becoming a repository of sensitive student docume=
nts.
The personal tracker is intended as a lightweight self-managed notebook, no=
t an
evidence vault.</p>

